// ASC physical pattern for unpacked float SF (no pack, no host permute).
// From Nightly per_block / per_token / per_channel ASC (sf_ub_dtype = f32
// when use_packed_ue8m0 is false). Full C++ is Nightly codegen; this is
// the pto.mi target.
//
// Row-major unpacked store of two f32 scales (ONEPT is ASC physical;
// VMI user code is a plain vstore of V<L x f32>):
//   S.vsts(sf_ub[sf_row, sf_j], scale01, dist='ONEPT_B32')
// pto.mi:
pto.mi.vsts %scale0, %sf_ub {dist = "ONEPT_B32"} : !pto.mi.vreg<64 x f32>
pto.mi.vsts %scale1, %sf_ub {dist = "ONEPT_B32"}

// TMA-col unpacked: same ONEPT store with transposed (col, row) address.
//   S.vsts(sf_ub[sf_j, sf_row], scale01, dist='ONEPT_B32')
// VMI must not require the host to permute GM into that layout.

// Unpacked load (rescale in-SF, per_channel L1):
%scale = pto.mi.vlds %sf_ub {dist = "BRC_B32"} : !pto.ptr<f32, ub> -> !pto.mi.vreg<64 x f32>
// ASC: S.vld(sf_ub[0, sf_j], dist='BRC_B32')

// Style contrast: desired VMI is vload/vstore of V<64 x f32>.
// pto.as owns ONEPT / BRC / TMA address. Host permute is not a port.
